## Implementation

### Change 1: Parallel topic analysis (cmd/hourstats/main.go)

In runAnalysisCycle(), immediately after the early return guards, start RunAnalysisCycle as a goroutine:

```go
// Start topic analysis in background (reads topic_tokens, 
// independent of hydration/sentiment/sparkline)
type topicResult struct{ err error }
topicCh := make(chan topicResult, 1)
if topicAnalyzer != nil {
    go func() {
        topicCh <- topicResult{err: topicAnalyzer.RunAnalysisCycle(ctx)}
    }()
}
```

After sparkline posting, collect the result:

```go
if topicAnalyzer != nil {
    tr := <-topicCh
    if tr.err != nil {
        slog.Error("topic analysis cycle failed", "error", tr.err)
    } else if sparkURI != "" && sparkCID != "" {
        if err := topicAnalyzer.RunTrendingPost(ctx, bskyClient, dryRun, 
            rootURI, rootCID, sparkURI, sparkCID); err != nil {
            slog.Error("trending post failed", "error", err)
        }
    } else {
        if err := topicAnalyzer.RunTrendingPost(ctx, bskyClient, dryRun, 
            "", "", "", ""); err != nil {
            slog.Error("trending post failed", "error", err)
        }
    }
}
```

Safety: RunAnalysisCycle uses only the DB store (SQLite WAL allows concurrent readers) and the Gemini HTTP client — no shared mutable state with the hydration/sparkline pipeline. RunTrendingPost still runs sequentially after both sparkline and analysis complete.

### Change 2: Parallel exemplar hydration (internal/topics/exemplar.go)

Replace the sequential for loop with concurrent goroutines:

- Launch one goroutine per non-meme topic
- Each goroutine queries GetExemplarCandidates independently
- Collect results via channel or slice with mutex
- Deduplicate usedHandles after all goroutines complete (process in rank order)

### Change 3: Add timing instrumentation

Log elapsed time at key boundaries so we can verify the improvement:
- Topic analysis goroutine start time
- Sparkline post complete time  
- Topic analysis goroutine result received time
- Trending post complete time

### Testing

- Verify topic analysis goroutine doesn't panic on early-return paths (corpus too small, no terms)
- Verify exemplar deduplication still works with parallel queries
- Verify SQLite WAL handles concurrent reads from topic analysis + hydration
- DRY_RUN mode should still work correctly (goroutine runs but trending post skips)
